4. API Endpoints
4.1 User APIs
    • POST /api/register – Register new user
    • POST /api/login – Authenticate user
    • GET /api/services – List available services
    • POST /api/book – Connect user to nearest available worker
4.2 Worker APIs
    • POST /api/worker/register – Worker signup
    • GET /api/worker/availability – Check availability status
    • POST /api/worker/update-location – Update worker location for live maps
    • GET /api/bookings – View incoming connections
4.3 Admin APIs (Optional Phase 2)
    • GET /api/admin/workers – View all workers
    • GET /api/admin/users – View all users
    • GET /api/admin/bookings – Monitor bookings and activity

5. Core Features (MVP)
User Features
    • Select service needed
    • Map view of nearby workers
    • Instant connection to worker
    • Worker ratings and reviews
Worker Features
    • Self-registration and profile setup
    • Update availability status
    • Update live location (optional)
    • Receive lead notifications
Admin Features
    • Dashboard to monitor users and workers
    • Track connections made

6. Technical Considerations
    1. Maps & Distance Calculation
        ◦ Use Haversine formula or Google Maps API to calculate nearby workers within radius
    2. Notifications
        ◦ Push notifications via Pusher or Firebase (optional MVP)
        ◦ SMS notifications for connections in Nigeria (Twilio, Africastalking)
    3. Security
        ◦ Password hashing (bcrypt)
        ◦ HTTPS for secure connections
        ◦ Role-based access (user / worker / admin)
    4. Scalability
        ◦ MVP: Host on shared cloud (DigitalOcean, AWS Lightsail)
        ◦ Later: Migrate to AWS or GCP for scaling

7. Deployment & Hosting
    • Domain: sharphand.ng
    • Frontend: Vue.js SPA hosted on Netlify / Vercel
    • Backend: Laravel API on DigitalOcean droplet / AWS EC2
    • Database: MySQL or PostgreSQL (cloud hosted for scalability)
    • Map API: Google Maps API key for geolocation and directions

8. Future Enhancements
    • In-app payments (Stripe / Flutterwave)
    • Worker subscription plans and featured listings
    • Ratings analytics & service history
    • Multi-city expansion
    • Mobile app (iOS/Android) via Ionic or React Native

✅ Summary:
SharpHand.ng is designed to be lightweight, fast, and hyper-local. The MVP focuses on connecting users to nearby workers instantly. Monetization and advanced features can be added later as the platform grows.

